===================
NOTICE
===================
	This source code is used for WET610N & WES610N. You can compile it and generate 
	firmware image by yourself, and upgrade firmware via webpage of WET610N & WES610N.
	For details, please refer below :

====================
Software requirement
====================

Operation System : Fedora 8

	Package Name			Version			Origin
	------------			-------			------
	GNU Compiler Collection (gcc)	3.4.6			ftp://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-3.4.6/gcc-3.4.6.tar.bz2
	GUN binutils			2.17			http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/binutils/binutils-2.17.tar.bz2
	uClibc				0.9.28.3		http://www.uclibc.org/downloads/old-releases/uClibc-0.9.28.3.tar.bz2
	GNU Make			3.80			http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/make/make-3.80.tar.gz
	lzma				4.32.5			ftp://ftp.pbone.net/mirror/archive.fedoraproject.org/fedora/linux/updates/8/i386.newkey/lzma-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm
	lzma-libs			4.32.5			ftp://ftp.pbone.net/mirror/archive.fedoraproject.org/fedora/linux/updates/8/i386.newkey/lzma-libs-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm


METHOD - 1:
===================
Compile instruction
===================

1. Use below URL to download Fedora 8, and install Fedora 8
	http://ftp.tcc.edu.tw/iso/RedHat-Fedora/8/i386/Fedora-8-i386-DVD.iso

2. Please use root privilege to login Fedora 8.

3. Setup compile environment:
	(1) Install Lzma: follow below steps to install it.
		[Command] :
    		wget ftp://ftp.pbone.net/mirror/archive.fedoraproject.org/fedora/linux/updates/8/i386.newkey/lzma-libs-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm
    		wget ftp://ftp.pbone.net/mirror/archive.fedoraproject.org/fedora/linux/updates/8/i386.newkey/lzma-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm
    		rpm -ivh lzma-libs-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm
    		rpm -ivh lzma-4.32.5-1.fc8.i386.rpm
    			
    	(2) To make sure you execute 'mke2fs' in any directory. please add the path of 'mke2fs' into $PATH
    		[Command]: 
    		#cd /
		#whereis mke2fs
		mke2fs: /sbin/mke2fs /etc/mke2fs.conf /usr/share/man/man8/mke2fs.8.gz
		#export PATH=$PATH:/sbin

4. Copy WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4_GPL.tgz into root directory and untar it. 
	Then enter folder of WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4 and type 'make' to compile code.
		[Command]:
    		cd /
    		cp [/dev/your flash device]/WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4_GPL.tgz . 
    		tar zxvf  WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4_GPL.tgz
    		cd WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4
		tar zxvf rootfs-star.tgz
	        make


5. After complete the make procedure, the firmware image 'WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4' will be generated at output folder.


METHOD - 2:   	
======================
Toolchain Compilation
======================

1. Compile toolchain: Actually, we should compile toolchain in Ubuntu-8.04.4.

	(1.) You can find the source code of arm-uclibc-3.4.6.tgz in the folder of toolchain.
	(2.) Please uncompress it, and follow text file of buildroot-howto.txt, and try to compile the toolchain.
      	(3.) After toolchain compilation completes, please enter the folder of tools and replace the folder of arm-uclibc-3.4.6 binaries with your new generated one.

Here are the steps to replace with the new toolchain binaries
	
2. When you get new toolchain of arm-linux-uclibc-3.4.6.tar.gz from U-buntu-8.04.4, please copy it into "WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4/tools" in Fedora-8.
	[Command]:
	cp [/dev/your flash device]/arm-linux-uclibc-3.4.6.tar.gz tools/
	cd tools
	rm -rf arm-uclibc-3.4.6/
	tar zxvf arm-linux-uclibc-3.4.6.tar.gz
	mv arm-linux-uclibc-3.4.6 arm-uclibc-3.4.6

3. Then you can compile the GPL code of WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4 using the above "compile instruction (method 1)" in Fedora 8
   the firmware image 'WET610N_v1.0.05_build_4' will be generated at output folder
   and the image size would be appr ~ 3MB
	

